Help Desk Lab 9: Windows Performance Troubleshooting
1. Incident Summary
Issue: Windows computer running slowly
Category: Windows Performance
Priority: Normal
Environment: Windows 11 (simulated lab)
Status: Troubleshooting plan identified; resolution requires verification
2. User-Reported Symptoms
The user reported slow computer performance. During troubleshooting, disk utilization fluctuated between approximately 52% and 91%. Windows Modules Installer was observed, and Windows displayed a prompt requesting a restart.

3. Troubleshooting Performed
Opened Task Manager to monitor disk utilization.
Observed fluctuating disk usage between approximately 52% and 91%.
Attempted to identify the process responsible for the highest disk usage; the exact process was not confirmed.
Observed Windows Modules Installer and a pending restart notification.
Selected the safe next step: save the user’s work, coordinate and perform the restart when appropriate, then reassess system performance.
4. Resolution Plan
Ensure all user work is saved.
Complete the requested restart when it is safe to do so.
Allow Windows updates or servicing operations to complete.
Reopen Task Manager and monitor disk utilization.
Identify the process responsible if high disk usage persists.
Confirm that system responsiveness has improved.
Escalate if the issue continues after appropriate troubleshooting.
5. Root Cause
Not yet confirmed. Windows servicing activity may have contributed to elevated disk usage, but additional investigation is required to establish the root cause.

6. Final Status
Troubleshooting decision: Correct
Restart: Recommended; completion not verified
Performance improvement: Not yet verified
Ticket status: Pending verification
7. Skills Demonstrated
Windows Task Manager
Disk utilization monitoring
Basic Windows update troubleshooting
Safe restart procedures
Process identification
Incident documentation
Root cause analysis and escalation
8. Key Takeaway
High disk utilization does not automatically indicate hardware failure or operating system corruption. A help desk technician should investigate the evidence, take safe corrective action, verify the outcome, and document any unresolved issues.
